          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-36308",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "disintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (becaus ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "disintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (because of an integer index out of range during a Grayscale call) via a crafted TIFF file to the scan function of scanner.go. NOTE: it is unclear whether there are common use cases in which this panic could have any security consequence"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36308",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-36308\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/disintegration/imaging\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2023-36308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36308)\ndisintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (because of an integer index out of range during a Grayscale call) via a crafted TIFF file to the scan function of scanner.go. NOTE: it is unclear whether there are common use cases in which this panic could have any security consequence",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-36308**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/disintegration/imaging||[CVE-2023-36308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36308)|\n\ndisintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (because of an integer index out of range during a Grayscale call) via a crafted TIFF file to the scan function of scanner.go. NOTE: it is unclear whether there are common use cases in which this panic could have any security consequence"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5932",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unmaintained, unsafe by design, and has known security issues"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GO-2026-5932\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: \nLink: [GO-2026-5932]()\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GO-2026-5932**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/crypto||[GO-2026-5932]()|\n\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46601",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/image/webp: golang.org/x/image/webp: Denial of Service via malformed VP8 chunk in WebP images"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The webp decoder can panic when processing a VP8 chunk with dimensions that do not match the canvas size."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46601",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46601\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: golang.org/x/image\nFixed Version: 0.43.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-46601](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46601)\nThe webp decoder can panic when processing a VP8 chunk with dimensions that do not match the canvas size.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46601**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|golang.org/x/image|0.43.0|[CVE-2026-46601](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46601)|\n\nThe webp decoder can panic when processing a VP8 chunk with dimensions that do not match the canvas size."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46602",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled im ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled images, permitting a malicious or corrupt image containing a very large tile to cause unbounded memory consumption."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46602",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46602\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/image\nFixed Version: 0.43.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-46602](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46602)\nThe TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled images, permitting a malicious or corrupt image containing a very large tile to cause unbounded memory consumption.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46602**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/image|0.43.0|[CVE-2026-46602](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46602)|\n\nThe TIFF decoder does not set a limit on the size of tiles in tiled images, permitting a malicious or corrupt image containing a very large tile to cause unbounded memory consumption."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46604",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder can panic when decoding an invalid image with an out- ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The TIFF decoder can panic when decoding an invalid image with an out-of-bounds strip offset."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46604",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46604\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/image\nFixed Version: 0.43.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-46604](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46604)\nThe TIFF decoder can panic when decoding an invalid image with an out-of-bounds strip offset.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46604**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/image|0.43.0|[CVE-2026-46604](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46604)|\n\nThe TIFF decoder can panic when decoding an invalid image with an out-of-bounds strip offset."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39822",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symli ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39822\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.12, 1.26.5, 1.27.0-rc.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-39822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822)\nOn Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39822**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|stdlib|1.25.12, 1.26.5, 1.27.0-rc.2|[CVE-2026-39822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822)|\n\nOn Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
